---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Chris Rooke — design systems, accessibility, and building for the web."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I work on design systems — the componentry, the tokens underneath it, and
      the shared language that makes a group of people build one product rather
      than several that happen to share a logo.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of what I find interesting sits at the seam between design and
      engineering: the point where a decision stops being a drawing and starts
      being an API that other teams have to live with. A token costs nothing to
      add and roughly forever to remove, and I think about that more than is
      strictly healthy.
    </p>

    <p>
      Accessibility is not a section of this page because it is not a section of
      the work. It is either in the component or it is a bug.
    </p>

    <h2>This site</h2>

    <p>
      Four kinds of thing live here.
      <a href="/projects">Projects</a> are case studies, sometimes with a series
      of posts attached. <a href="/writing">Writing</a> is the long-form.
      <a href="/notes">Notes</a> are short and often untitled, and
      <a href="/stash">Stash</a> is what I have been reading, watching and
      listening to. The last two share a feed on the homepage because they
      genuinely interleave.
    </p>

    <p>
      There is an <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> covering all of it, a
      <a href="/sitemap">sitemap</a> if you would rather browse, and a
      <a href="/colophon">colophon</a> describing how the thing is built.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
